#
# Conformance case: profiles/goal-rdf-list-functions (#1009 §5)
# AC: the native reasoning layer backs the binary RDF list predicates by walking
# the rdf:first/rdf:rest chain. gmeow:listContains and gmeow:listLength are
# executably covered under the ProceduralPrologProfile: the query fixtures recurse
# over rdf:first/rdf:rest and list length uses the native arithmetic builtin
# (`N is M + 1`). Over the list (x y z) at l0, membership returns {x, y, z},
# absent membership returns no answers, length returns 3, and the empty list
# returns 0.
#
# The listGet/listIndexOf ternary arithmetic programs and the listSlice/listConcat
# variants formerly depended on the retired SLD fallback. They are no longer
# claimed by this executable case: an equivalent n-ary arithmetic query receives
# the production dispatcher's typed unsupported-fragment error. Their FnO terms
# remain declarative projection vocabulary, not an executable-runtime claim.
#
# No forward rules: the list EDB lives in input.nq; the list operations are the
# backward goals in queries/.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/profiles/goal-rdf-list-functions/> .

# Schema: the element sort used by the projection back-ends.
ex:Element a logic:Kind .
